t(7, 830, """The narration was cited by Imam Nu'aym ibn Hammad in the book "[al-Fitan]", and was also narrated by Imam al-Hakim in al-Mustadrak ala al-Sahihayn.

The hadith is narrated from the noble Companion Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him) (the keeper of the secrets of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the trials and the hypocrites).

The text of the narration and its explanation:
From Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:
"My Ummah will not perish until there appear among them tamayuz, tamayul and ma'ami'."

When Hudhayfah heard these words, he asked the Prophet ﷺ about them.

I said: O Prophet of Allah, what is tamayuz?
He ﷺ said: "Partisanship that people will introduce into Islam after me."

(Tamayuz) here is dividing the ranks of Muslims on the basis of narrow identities (such as Shu'ubiyya, extreme nationalism, ethnic racism and tribalism) after Islam had fused them into one identity.
I said: Then what is tamayul?
He ﷺ said: "A tribe leans against a tribe and deems its sanctity lawful, unjustly."
That is, a sect, state or tribe takes sides against another, so the intellectual and verbal division turns into military and economic aggression and the making lawful of blood and property.
I said: Then what is ma'ami'?
He ﷺ said: "The cities marching against one another, and their necks clashing in war."
(The amsar) are the states; what is meant is the armies and peoples of the Muslims clashing in grinding internal wars in which they strike one another's necks.
------------------------------
The grade of the hadith from the scholarly side:
The ruling of the scholars:
The hadith has weakness in its chains (it contains a narrator called Sa'id ibn Sinan, whom hadith scholars such as al-Hafiz al-Dhahabi declared weak).

A note on reality: Despite the weakness of its chain, the scholars of the Ummah pointed out that its meaning and its confirmation have, sadly, come true in the history of the Muslims through the emergence of regional partisanships and mutually hostile nationalisms, and internal wars in the past and possibly at the end of time.""")

h(7, 2300, """Peoples have come to curse one another, and the Infallible ﷺ foretold this!""")

